{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Until</b> — The men of your covenant could not save you; rather they sent you to the border's edge, your fugitives going into captivity." "<b>Your bread</b> — When you were in your place, this is 'under you.'" "<b>The men of your peace</b> — Those who feed you are the ones who put poison in your bread, and you did not perceive it." "<b>And a trap</b> — Like מזורו (his trap). And a כ is missing from the word אין, like 'a man who has no understanding in him.' And like it: ולאין אונים עצמה ירבה ולאיש אין אונים. And Rabbi Marinus said: בו is like ממנו (from him), as in וכל ערל לא יאכל בו — 'you did not perceive from him.'"], :book :obadiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {3 "Reading הרגשת as 'you did not perceive it' (לא הרגשת); possible corruption of לא הרגשת בו at the end, where the subject shifts; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Obadiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=18&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:33.088405250Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}